{"name":"The Fang Grey","hex":"#436174","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fang","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, pointed canine tooth used for biting and tearing flesh. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Synonym of mandible, the long mouthpart of insects and other invertebrates."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike or attack with the fangs.","To enable to catch or tear; to furnish with fangs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fang"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fang","blocks":[{"text":"A fang is a long, pointed tooth. In mammals, a fang is a modified maxillary tooth, used for biting and tearing flesh. In snakes, it is a specialized tooth that is associated with a venom gland. Spiders also have external fangs, which are part of the chelicerae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg/330px-Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fang"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Halloween95_Showing_my_fangs.jpg/500px-Halloween95_Showing